      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$ on $M?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim{\\small \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 4+(2)(5) & 1+(2)(-3) & -5+(2)(-1) \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 14 & -5 & -7 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
